The main changes I made to fix the error:

1. Changed the language.translate implementation from a string to an actual function in the JSON data
2. Added proper parsing of the state values before passing them to the component
3. Ensured that the translate functions are properly set after parsing the JSON
4. Used proper function implementations instead of string representations for the translate function

The error was occurring because when we JSON.stringify a function, it gets lost in the serialization. By providing actual functions after parsing the JSON data, we ensure that the translate function is available and callable when the component needs it.

This should resolve the "t is not a function" error while maintaining the functionality of the preview component.

